<title>POLAND: COMPUTERLAND STOCK OPTION ISSUE CLEARED.</title>
<headline>COMPUTERLAND STOCK OPTION ISSUE CLEARED.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade 273,897 new shares in software firm ComputerLand SA to be offered to management and employees in a stock option, the firm's president said.</p>
<p>Tomasz Sielicki told journalists after a commission meeting on Thursday that next month 207,897 shares would be offered management and 66,000 shares to about 10 other top employees.</p>
<p>The firm currently has 4,862,760 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
